  "notes": "Hand-transcribed 2026-10-02 from the official Butler University Jordan College of the Arts 'B.A. IN MUSIC PLUS A SECONDARY MAJOR IN MUSIC INDUSTRY STUDIES' plan (FA_25 version). Semester totals match the PDF's stated totals (17/16/14/15/15-16/17/15/18); the plan total is 127 credits using the 2-credit MT 440 option for the 'AC 203, EC 231, or MT 440 (2-3 credits)' slot - with AC 203/EC 231 (3 credits) the total is 128. That slot and the Communication-and-Culture elective and MI 353/355/357 slots are modeled as choice slots with the PDF's own option lists. NOTE from the source: the 8-semester sequence includes 4 additional semesters of Applied Music (8 credits) and 2 additional semesters of Major Ensemble (2 credits) beyond the BA Music requirements; most music majors take these for scholarship reasons. So applied study (AM __) appears 8 semesters x 2 = 16 and Major Ensemble (ES __) 8 semesters x 1 = 8; allow_repeated_courses is set and documented here. Communication and Culture elective options per the source: CCM 254, CCM 330, CCM 376, CCM 420, CCM 468, CCM 470, CCM 481, CCM 482, JR 325, JR 417, SLHS 338, SPM 458, STR 405. MI elective options: MI 353 Audio for Video, MI 355 The Live Entertainment Industry, MI 357 Experiential Application. The double major fulfills the Perspectives of the Creative Arts and Social World core areas; music majors fulfill BCR via arts event attendance; the Indianapolis Community Requirement is NOT satisfied by this combination. Piano majors substitute AM 031/032 plus two credits of music electives for AM 021-024 (the sequence shows AM 021-024). Prerequisites are not listed in the plan; prereq arrays are empty (chains live in the Bulletin course descriptions).",
